    "body": "claimed: Claude Code session sweep-query (for dylanoliverdo-coder) · 2026-11-26T13:19Z · branch issue/4182-stl-as-written · plan: (1) the stock export judges the mesh as written: corners rounded to their f32 values, welded bit-exact with `repair::weld` when a facet collapses there, `unpaired_edges` on that result, then write or refuse by name; a mesh with nothing to collapse writes byte-identical. (2) `drop_degenerate` keeps a duplicate set by edge parity: no copy when the rest of the mesh uses its edges an even number of times, one when odd. A back-to-back pair left by a collapse then goes, and a stray duplicate on a closed solid keeps one, as `weld_drops_collapsed_zero_area_and_duplicate_triangles` pins today. Plain \"k mod 2\" would drop that real face. Pins: the two synthetic cases in the issue, and a clean mesh written byte-identical.\n\nThis issue was drafted and filed by an agent (Claude Code), so it should carry `source:agent`; our suggestion for the rest is `bug`, `area:sim`, `area:geometry`, `P3`, `effort:high` (geometry and stock simulation, the safety floor). We cannot set labels or assign; could a collaborator set them?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
